---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { faqPageSchema } from '../../lib/schema';
const faqSchema = faqPageSchema([
  { question: 'macOS Ghidra 12.1.4 native decompiler missing', answer: 'Ghidra 12.1.4 PUBLIC ships linux/win decompilers only — macOS doctor reports native_decompiler missing; community make ghidra_opt recipe. BYO toolchain.' },
]);
---
<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="macOS Ghidra 12.1.4 native decompiler missing | rea.run"
  description="Ghidra 12.1.4 PUBLIC ships linux/win decompilers only — macOS doctor reports native_decompiler missing; community make ghidra_opt recipe. BYO toolchain."
  path="/faq/macos-ghidra-decompiler/"
  schema={faqSchema}
>
  <article class="prose-page mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14">
    <p class="text-sm"><a class="quiet-link" href="/faq/">← FAQ hub</a></p>
    <p class="badge badge-accent mt-4">FAQ · P0</p>
    <h1 class="display mt-4 text-4xl text-[var(--color-ink)]">macOS: Ghidra native decompiler missing (12.1.4)</h1>
    <p class="lede mt-4 !max-w-none">If <code>doctor --provider ghidra</code> fails on Mac with <code>native_decompiler</code> missing, you are often hitting a packaging gap — not a broken npm install.</p>

    <h2>What happens</h2>
    <p>Ghidra <strong>12.1.4 PUBLIC</strong> distributions commonly ship native decompiler binaries for <code>linux_x86_64</code> and <code>win_x86_64</code> only. On macOS, REA’s doctor can report the decompiler OS folder empty/missing. Upstream REA <strong>refuses to auto-build</strong> that native tool for you.</p>

    <h2>What to do (community recipe)</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Confirm JDK + <code>GHIDRA_INSTALL_DIR</code> with absolute paths.</li>
      <li>Build the optional decompiler from Ghidra sources using the documented <code>make ghidra_opt</code> (or current upstream equivalent) on your Mac toolchain.</li>
      <li>Copy the resulting <code>decompile</code> binary into Ghidra’s <code>os/mac_x86_64/</code> (or <code>mac_arm_64/</code> as appropriate) layout.</li>
      <li>Re-run <code>npx -y rea-agents@latest doctor --provider ghidra --json</code>. Pair with launch diagnostics from related issues when the GUI/headless wrapper also misreports.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Exact make targets move with Ghidra versions — verify against Ghidra’s own build docs for your tag. This site will not paste proprietary plugin cracks.</p>

    <h2>Related</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/docs/windows-ghidra/">Windows × Ghidra wiring</a> (sibling host story)</li>
      <li><a href="/docs/ghidra-large-binaries/">Large binaries &amp; deadlines</a></li>
      <li><a href="/faq/setup-vs-providers/">Setup vs providers</a></li>
    </ul>

    <footer class="mt-12 border-t border-[var(--color-line)] pt-6 text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] not-prose">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">Sources</p>
      <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5 text-xs">
        <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/issues/1994" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Issue #1994 — macOS native_decompiler missing (@EDMND-SRC)</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/issues/1992" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Issue #1992 — launch diagnostics</a></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-4"><a class="quiet-link" href="/compliance/">Compliance</a> · BYO toolchain only; no piracy of proprietary plugins.</p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
